; MasterCard DMA test disk: tests mastercard.device on the real card.
; Reads only. The buffer tests write the drive's own buffer, not the disk.
; For the disk write tests, run: Execute S:write-test
FailAt 21
MakeDir RAM:T
Assign T: RAM:T
Echo "MasterCard DMA test - reads only, logging to RAM during MCDiag."
Echo "Taking over from the M-Tec ROM driver. Don't use the hard disk until you reboot."
MCDiag TAKEOVER LOG RAM:mcdiag.log
Type RAM:mcdiag.log >DF0:mcdiag.log
Set u `MCDiag FINDUNIT`
Echo "== devtest on unit $u" >>DF0:mcdiag.log
devtest -p mastercard.device >>DF0:mcdiag.log
devtest -g mastercard.device $u >>DF0:mcdiag.log
devtest -t mastercard.device $u >>DF0:mcdiag.log
devtest -bb mastercard.device $u >>DF0:mcdiag.log
Echo "== done" >>DF0:mcdiag.log
Echo "Done. The log is DF0:mcdiag.log (More DF0:mcdiag.log)."
Echo "Optional: Execute S:write-test, which writes near the end of the disk and restores it."
Echo "Experimental: Execute S:sync-test (read-only 5 MB/s offset-4 sync, then resets async)."
